  "board.quote.name": "Uncle Bob Martin",
  "board.quote.handle": "@unclebobmartin · 5 oct 2026",
  "board.quote.text": "Se supone que los ingenieros de software deben hacer exactamente lo que\nsiempre hemos hecho. Asegurar que la composición y la estructura del\nsistema sean robustas y mantenibles y que el comportamiento del sistema\nsirva adecuadamente a las necesidades de nuestros usuarios.\n\nEsto requiere disciplina de ingeniería. No tiene por qué requerir una\nlectura detallada del código; igual que usar compiladores no requiere\nuna lectura detallada del binario.",
  "board.site.url": "platform.plainconcepts.com",
  "board.tree.file": "your-repo/ · after the install",
  "board.tree.code": "├─ AGENTS.md\talways in context\n├─ ARCHITECTURE.md\tgenerated from the code\n├─ DESIGN.md\tgenerated from the design system\n├─ opencode.jsonc\tOpenCode config · MCP servers\n├─ openspec/\tproposal · specs · tasks\n├─ .agents/skills/\n│  ├─ pc-guardrails-generic\tevery agent loads it\n│  ├─ pc-guardrails-project\tyour rules, from /make-guardrails\n│  ├─ pc-plan-goal\texplore → propose → apply → archive\n│  └─ pc-…\tonly what this project needs\n└─ .opencode/\n   ├─ agents/\tfullstack-engineer · *-engineer\n   ├─ commands/\t/plan-goal · /repo-verify · …\n   ├─ plugins/\tpc-system-reminders blocks unsafe calls\n   ├─ scripts/check-diff.mjs\trefuses AI slop in a diff\n   └─ harness.json\tupdate replays your answers",
  "board.quote.source": "x.com/unclebobmartin · traducido",
  "board.markdown.file": ".github/workflows/implement-issue.md",
  "board.markdown.code": "---\non:\n  issues:\n    types: [labeled]\npermissions: read-all\nengine: claude\nsafe-outputs:\n  create-pull-request:\n---\n\n# Implement the issue\n\nRead issue #${{ github.event.issue.number }}.\nChange the code so it does what the issue asks.\nRun the tests, then open one pull request.",
